From 5b041f64fbf188aca027c9a38707ddf5f39eaf49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:17:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(fairness): validate complete fleet roster evidence
 [daveey]

Inventory tree scans only describe respondents, not complete fleet coverage.
Add a read-only roster manifest validator and inventory roster CLI that keeps
expected/opening/closing/coverage source identities separate, retains unknowns,
and refuses duplicates, offline sources, gaps and changing membership.

Identity is gateway/profile/board UID/database UID; serving process, source and
config pins must agree with capture receipts. Membership continuity requires
its own receipt rather than inference from equal endpoint lists. Version 1
explicitly refuses changing membership rather than inventing join coverage.

No scheduler/capture activation, replay, policy changes or fairness claims.
The full report coverage consumer is owned by the sibling Phase A gate task;
this standalone validator does not silently mutate an existing capture.

Tests cover complete, omitted, duplicate, offline, changing and malformed
rosters plus the real operator CLI. Read-only current discovery intentionally
validates INDETERMINATE because no authorized capture window or process/cut
attestations exist. Registry eligibility is not proof of actual serving.
